Apple today released iOS 26.3.1 and iPadOS 26.3.1, minor updates to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-26/">iPadOS 26</a> operating systems. The software comes three weeks after Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/02/11/apple-releases-ios-26-3-and-ipados-26-3/">released iOS 26.3 and iPadOS 26.3</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1037114" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/iOS-26.3.1-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" /><br/>
The new software can be downloaded on eligible iPhones and iPads over-the-air by going to Settings > General > Software Update.<br/>
<br/>
According to Apple's release notes, the update adds support for the new Studio Display and Studio Display XDR, and it includes unspecified bug fixes. <br/>
<br/>
